---
id: port_price_crash
title: Market Volatility
tags: [trade, event]
context: port
weight: 7
cooldown: 6
---

=== intro

The market alerts cascade through your systems—prices 
shifting, opportunities appearing, chaos in the exchanges.

Something has disrupted supply lines. A Sera incursion, 
maybe. A major contract falling through. The cause 
doesn't matter. What matters is the opportunity.

Prices are moving fast. You need to decide faster.

* [Buy commodities before prices rise]
  { credits >= 80 }
  -> buy

* [Sell cargo before prices fall]
  { cargo.mineral }
  -> sell

* [Wait and watch]
  ~ chronicle "Market Volatility"
    Market disruption. Watched prices swing. Didn't act fast enough.
  -> END

=== buy

You dump credits into the market, buying whatever's 
undervalued before the rest of the traders catch on.

The timing is good. Prices stabilize higher than you 
paid. Profit.

* [Secure the goods]
  ~ credits -= 80
  ~ addCard cargo_refined_metals
  ~ addCard cargo_common_components
  ~ chronicle "Market Play"
    Bought commodities during a market dip. Good timing.
  -> END

=== sell

You move fast, liquidating cargo before the price floor 
drops. Other traders are doing the same—it's a race to 
the exits.

You make it out ahead. Not maximum value, but better 
than holding through the crash.

* [Take the credits]
  ~ credits += 50
  ~ chronicle "Market Play"
    Sold cargo during market volatility. Got out before the crash.
  -> END
